      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T16:21:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t been able to figure out how to fix the assembly generated by the compiler. From what I can tell, the intent here is to use the clobber register list to preserve the registers in the clobber list since we\u0027re saving them into https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/36cc38e1818e384b350b809069620594fbcc6664/include/panic.h#53.\n\nHowever, looking at the registers that are saved (https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/36cc38e1818e384b350b809069620594fbcc6664/include/panic.h#34), we never actually save R3 (and immediately clobber it with the \"mov r3, sp\" instruction in the inline assembly), so I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary to include R3 at all in the clobber list. In that case we can just remove it from the list (for both compilers), but I wasn\u0027t sure if I was missing something.\n\nDoes my understanding sound correct? Should I try loosening the constraints so that the clobber list only includes registers in: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/36cc38e1818e384b350b809069620594fbcc6664/include/panic.h#34 ?",
      "parentUuid": "95d2b9d6_37ebb90c",
