      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T22:29:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think we can clobber r0, r1, r2, r3 because they\u0027re saved in the exception frame. r4, r5 are also clobbered (after saved to pregs). So, I think we should have r0 ~ r5, cc, memory and remove the rest. Does it work?\n\nThis compiles, but it\u0027s unclear whether it will behave correctly. See next comment.\n\n\u003e since that they are not clobbered\n\nI think the issue is that in that case the compiler can potentially use (clobber) those registers when generating the assembly for exception_panic. In that case, the values in those registers that we save would not be correct (they would not be the original values from entering exception_panic). For example, it can decide to use r6 for \"pregs\" or \"pstack\". Looking at the assembly, that\u0027s exactly what it does:\n\n 00000000 \u003cexception_panic\u003e:\n   0:   4808            ldr     r0, [pc, #32]   ; (24 \u003cexception_panic+0x24\u003e)\n   2:   4e09            ldr     r6, [pc, #36]   ; (28 \u003cexception_panic+0x28\u003e)\n   4:   f3ef 8109       mrs     r1, PSP\n   8:   f3ef 8205       mrs     r2, IPSR\n   c:   466b            mov     r3, sp\n   e:   c0fe            stmia   r0!, {r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7}\n  10:   4641            mov     r1, r8\n  12:   464a            mov     r2, r9\n  14:   4653            mov     r3, sl\n  16:   465c            mov     r4, fp\n  18:   4675            mov     r5, lr\n  1a:   c03e            stmia   r0!, {r1, r2, r3, r4, r5}\n  1c:   46b5            mov     sp, r6\n  1e:   f7ff fffe       bl      0 \u003cexception_panic\u003e\n  22:   46c0            nop                     ; (mov r8, r8)\n  24:   20003f74        .word   0x20003f74\n  28:   20003f70        .word   0x20003f70",
      "parentUuid": "0975ba3c_6725dd57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
