      "writtenOn": "2021-11-13T00:49:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Extended-Asm.html#InputOperands:\n\nasm asm-qualifiers ( AssemblerTemplate \n                      : OutputOperands\n                      : InputOperands\n                      : Clobbers\n                      : GotoLabels)\n                      \nIt seems registers aren\u0027t allowed to be in InputOperands. (Otherwise, we can list r4 ~ r11 there). IIUC, Clobbers prevents GCC from using the values in those regs AFTER the assembly. So, my guess is Clobbers can make GCC refrain from using r4 ~ r11 BEFORE the assembly because they can\u0027t be used after the assembly without reinitialization.\n\nIf this is the case, we can remove r0, r1, r2, r3 from Clobbers. I got the following:\n\nldr     r3, [pc, #32]   ; (800c254 \u003cexception_panic+0x24\u003e)\nldr     r2, [pc, #36]   ; (800c258 \u003cexception_panic+0x28\u003e)\nadds    r0, r3, #0\nmrs     r1, PSP\nmrs     r2, IPSR\nmov     r3, sp\nstmia   r0!, {r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7}\nmov     r1, r8\nmov     r2, r9\nmov     r3, sl\nmov     r4, fp\nmov     r5, lr\nstmia   r0!, {r1, r2, r3, r4, r5}\nmov     sp, r2\nbl      80121ec \u003creport_panic\u003e\n.word   0x20003f74\n.word   0x20003f70\n\nWDYT? How does clang like it?\n\nWe need a test for this. Set some magic values in each regs and read them back after crash.",
      "parentUuid": "94fe05f9_a1152732",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 8
      },
